  "status": "verified-sample",
  "coverage": "complete",
  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 55 actions (18 in src/actions.ts, 37 in the table commonActions in src/actions/common.ts) and 4 feedbacks (3 boolean feedbacks generated from src/state.ts booleanProperties, plus the advanced feedback \"image\").",
    "Actions in src/actions/common.ts are built from a table (Definition objects and the fixed() helper). Their ids, names and options come from that table; provenance points to the table row (for fixed() rows the line of the fixed(...) call).",
    "Actions marked with a \"handle\" in the source get two leading options: handleMode (userNumber, titanId, location) and handle (text, variables allowed). Runtime validation in src/api/commands.ts handleParams: userNumber must match ^\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$ and be > 0, titanId must be a positive integer, location must match ^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*_\\d+_\\d+$ (for example playback_2_1). Invalid values are logged and the action does nothing; the catalog records the handle option as free text.",
    "The three boolean feedbacks (blackout, blind, highlight) are registered in a loop (src/feedbacks.ts:9) over booleanProperties (src/state.ts:2-4, member names Masters.IsDeskBlackedOut, Programmer.BlindActive, Programmer.Editor.Fixtures.Highlight). The module description says the state is refreshed about every 5 seconds.",
    "Several actions share the option ids \"un\" (user number, 1-9999) and \"ft\"/\"masterft\" (fade time and use-master-fade-time). cuelistSetNextCue uses a text field \"cn\" (variables allowed, runtime range 1-9999); the other cue actions use numbers.",
    "The lock/unlock and timeline-reset fields (LOCK_ACTION, PASSWORD, RESETIFPLAYING in src/fields.ts) are defined but used by no action in this commit and are therefore not catalogued.",
    "Several write actions are state-changing on a live show (blackoutDesk, freezeDmx, releaseAllPlaybacks, programmerClear). The catalog only describes them.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.11.3: options do not support expressions."
  ],
